{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$U_j$", "MATH_0007": "$U_j \\to T$", "MATH_0008": "$U_j$", "MATH_0009": "$T_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-definition-smooth}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-smooth-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1d10415810964e88b181b69e6405fb79372da47c1f1dd148e5245b96f54c77b3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3494f76c471922c623093dd75289feb734d40feb0a662300bcd376b8af81e0a7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a smooth covering of <MATH_0003>.\nThen there exists a smooth covering\n<MATH_0004> which is a refinement\nof <MATH_0005> such that each <MATH_0006> is an affine\nscheme, and such that each morphism <MATH_0007> is standard\nsmooth, see Morphisms, Definition <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, we may choose each <MATH_0008> to be open affine in one of the <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4dd2a547e4ab4f0b0d75a595290db710f5be0e8364c41e53a18a2cf82c492968", "unit_id": "tag:0222:statement"}
